start the core on the panel's blank

SLOT_DRIVE_EMU=overlap: each present ticks the core and draws the frame the
previous tick produced, instead of waiting up to 12 ms for this tick's.

Unchained (SLOT_DRIVE_EMU=0, the card's default) the core keeps a 60 Hz
timer on a 100 Hz kernel tick, against a panel at 59.6 Hz, so its frames
reach the display unevenly: some are shown twice and some never. Super
Mario World on the Flip, rewind off, traced 7 of 600 presents missing a
latch while still visibly hitching. Chained the old way (SLOT_DRIVE_EMU=1)
the core's 8 ms and the draw's 6 ms run in series and 330-510 of 600
presents missed, measured 2026-10-30, stock 202510011046.

Overlapped, the core runs on the second CPU while this one draws, and its
clock is the panel's. The cost is one frame of latency. Opt-in from the
card until it has been measured on the handheld.

Applies on top of 0028, upstream 91499a9.

